    {
      "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:fdcb393d2609cd5ca001f731d7de4e80f30fea1dae2f66e2182330e13876a601",
      "@type": "rkaf:Artifact",
      "rkaf:hasArtifactIdentifier": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:fdcb393d2609cd5ca001f731d7de4e80f30fea1dae2f66e2182330e13876a601",
      "rkaf:artifactIdentifierScheme": "rkaf:urn-persistent",
      "rkaf:hasContentDigest": "sha256:eb41314a7c766ad60099e27fde73549a5d3e3213059276e71bb62dc9bc6a3d6c",
      "dcterms:format": "application/json",
      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:bc8f2644e5c764be5d229814a5a33628adf53656c84acdc2c042c2c7e7a676a3\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:3799914782a2ce75bdc348e3908ab5f034d943715cccb8701431c48ebfbd496a\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:d164868dc3fe62b5b82baea79cb2913b922a96b878e982e8a68e200665ebf1b1\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:886c241ffd4fe82163686c62e0bfd6f5acd825ebed1c1570d4a1893e0b132fb6\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:44e36fba2d76def81b6767ca9243bceed36859f839b42044b739f9bff849a30c\"],\"choice_quote\":\"\",\"choice_text\":\"\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[\"(2) Has been employed for at least 1,250 hours of service during the 12-month period immediately preceding the commencement of the leave ( see § 825.801 for special hours of service requirements for airline flight crew employees), and\",\"(c)(1) Except as provided in paragraph (c)(2) of this section and in § 825.801 containing the special hours of service requirement for airline flight crew employees, whether an employee has worked the minimum 1,250 hours of service is determined according to the principles established under the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) for determining compensable hours of work. See 29 CFR part 785. The determining factor is the number of hours an employee has worked for the employer within the meaning of the FLSA. The determination is not limited by methods of recordkeeping, or by compensation agreements that do not accurately reflect all of the hours an employee has worked for or been in service to the employer. Any accurate accounting of actual hours worked under FLSA's principles may be used.\"],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":4438,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":4438,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:3604:4438:sha256-7dbcb059fc78a2f697d27032e4d0f71484bebb06578094a6d4adecf70f95a027\",\"quote\":\"(2) An employee returning from USERRA-covered service shall be credited with the hours of service that would have been performed but for the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service in determining the employee's eligibility for FMLA-qualifying leave. Accordingly, a person reemployed following USERRA-covered service has the hours that would have been worked for the employer added to any hours actually worked during the previous 12-month period to meet the hours of service requirement. In order to determine the hours that would have been worked during the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service, the employee's pre-service work schedule can generally be used for calculations. See § 825.801(c) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees.\",\"start\":3604},{\"end\":4438,\"field\":\"logic_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:3604:4438:sha256-7dbcb059fc78a2f697d27032e4d0f71484bebb06578094a6d4adecf70f95a027\",\"quote\":\"(2) An employee returning from USERRA-covered service shall be credited with the hours of service that would have been performed but for the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service in determining the employee's eligibility for FMLA-qualifying leave. Accordingly, a person reemployed following USERRA-covered service has the hours that would have been worked for the employer added to any hours actually worked during the previous 12-month period to meet the hours of service requirement. In order to determine the hours that would have been worked during the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service, the employee's pre-service work schedule can generally be used for calculations. See § 825.801(c) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees.\",\"start\":3604},{\"end\":3663,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:3658:3663:sha256-56ee5b508706bf2de91712d85d6d1e11ddbff01949142ed6e8c22e3b1bed1c71\",\"quote\":\"shall\",\"start\":3658},{\"end\":4438,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:3604:4438:sha256-7dbcb059fc78a2f697d27032e4d0f71484bebb06578094a6d4adecf70f95a027\",\"quote\":\"(2) An employee returning from USERRA-covered service shall be credited with the hours of service that would have been performed but for the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service in determining the employee's eligibility for FMLA-qualifying leave. Accordingly, a person reemployed following USERRA-covered service has the hours that would have been worked for the employer added to any hours actually worked during the previous 12-month period to meet the hours of service requirement. In order to determine the hours that would have been worked during the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service, the employee's pre-service work schedule can generally be used for calculations. See § 825.801(c) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees.\",\"start\":3604},{\"end\":406,\"field\":\"context:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:172:406:sha256-f8c620c940dc57284f54426aad3bc219080834d541b71563d59c69ce9eeffe60\",\"quote\":\"(2) Has been employed for at least 1,250 hours of service during the 12-month period immediately preceding the commencement of the leave ( see § 825.801 for special hours of service requirements for airline flight crew employees), and\",\"start\":172},{\"end\":3602,\"field\":\"context:1\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:2806:3602:sha256-0207e56b05e1baa2b73068ae0df66fa509d96f5833d29bab4fe4be2d62b8fd28\",\"quote\":\"(c)(1) Except as provided in paragraph (c)(2) of this section and in § 825.801 containing the special hours of service requirement for airline flight crew employees, whether an employee has worked the minimum 1,250 hours of service is determined according to the principles established under the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) for determining compensable hours of work. See 29 CFR part 785. The determining factor is the number of hours an employee has worked for the employer within the meaning of the FLSA. The determination is not limited by methods of recordkeeping, or by compensation agreements that do not accurately reflect all of the hours an employee has worked for or been in service to the employer. Any accurate accounting of actual hours worked under FLSA's principles may be used.\",\"start\":2806}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:fdcb393d2609cd5ca001f731d7de4e80f30fea1dae2f66e2182330e13876a601\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"(2) An employee returning from USERRA-covered service shall be credited with the hours of service that would have been performed but for the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service in determining the employee's eligibility for FMLA-qualifying leave. Accordingly, a person reemployed following USERRA-covered service has the hours that would have been worked for the employer added to any hours actually worked during the previous 12-month period to meet the hours of service requirement. In order to determine the hours that would have been worked during the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service, the employee's pre-service work schedule can generally be used for calculations. See § 825.801(c) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees.\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:44e36fba2d76def81b6767ca9243bceed36859f839b42044b739f9bff849a30c\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"shall\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:b17be813de6a04a93f7da455c4a2046d48ab206cec659bfd79470a765fe6b02c\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(2) An employee returning from USERRA-covered service shall be credited with the hours of service that would have been performed but for the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service in determining the employee's eligibility for FMLA-qualifying leave. Accordingly, a person reemployed following USERRA-covered service has the hours that would have been worked for the employer added to any hours actually worked during the previous 12-month period to meet the hours of service requirement. In order to determine the hours that would have been worked during the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service, the employee's pre-service work schedule can generally be used for calculations. See § 825.801(c) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees.\",\"references\":[\"§ 825.801(c)\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:add89cc12789542228ad017dac2a85cbfb7182e11d2e6aa851273ba8268715de\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(2) An employee returning from USERRA-covered service shall be credited with the hours of service that would have been performed but for the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service in determining the employee's eligibility for FMLA-qualifying leave. Accordingly, a person reemployed following USERRA-covered service has the hours that would have been worked for the employer added to any hours actually worked during the previous 12-month period to meet the hours of service requirement. In order to determine the hours that would have been worked during the period of absence from work due to or necessitated by USERRA-covered service, the employee's pre-service work schedule can generally be used for calculations. See § 825.801(c) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees.\"],\"scope_text\":\"Determining FMLA leave eligibility for an employee returning from or reemployed following USERRA-covered service.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":3604,\"summary\":\"An employee returning from USERRA-covered service shall be credited with the hours of service that would have been performed but for the absence necessitated by USERRA-covered service, added to hours actually worked during the previous 12-month period, and the employee's pre-service work schedule can generally be used for calculations.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
      "dcterms:references": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:bc8f2644e5c764be5d229814a5a33628adf53656c84acdc2c042c2c7e7a676a3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:3799914782a2ce75bdc348e3908ab5f034d943715cccb8701431c48ebfbd496a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:d164868dc3fe62b5b82baea79cb2913b922a96b878e982e8a68e200665ebf1b1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:886c241ffd4fe82163686c62e0bfd6f5acd825ebed1c1570d4a1893e0b132fb6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:44e36fba2d76def81b6767ca9243bceed36859f839b42044b739f9bff849a30c"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:4440:5368:sha256-f224bb89288a47851c4a1b3b1e2aceb37d95d77172afee44175f2f36b851f8ae",
      "@type": "rkaf:SourceFragment",
      "oa:hasSource": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:a4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f",
      "rkaf:fragmentIdentityScheme": "rkaf:carrier-local-fragment",
      "rkaf:sourceArtifactDigest": "sha256:a4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f",
      "rkaf:fragmentContentDigest": "sha256:f224bb89288a47851c4a1b3b1e2aceb37d95d77172afee44175f2f36b851f8ae",
      "rkaf:selectorKind": [
        "oa:TextQuoteSelector",
        "oa:TextPositionSelector"
      ],
      "oa:hasSelector": [
        {
          "@type": "oa:TextQuoteSelector",
          "oa:exact": "(3) In the event an employer does not maintain an accurate record of hours worked by an employee, including for employees who are exempt from FLSA's requirement that a record be kept of their hours worked (e.g., bona fide executive, administrative, and professional employees as defined in FLSA Regulations, 29 CFR part 541), the employer has the burden of showing that the employee has not worked the requisite hours. An employer must be able to clearly demonstrate, for example, that full-time teachers ( see § 825.102 for definition) of an elementary or secondary school system, or institution of higher education, or other educational establishment or institution (who often work outside the classroom or at their homes) did not work 1,250 hours during the previous 12 months in order to claim that the teachers are not eligible for FMLA leave. See § 825.801(d) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees."
        },
        {
          "@type": "oa:TextPositionSelector",
          "oa:start": 4440,
          "oa:end": 5368,
          "rkaf:coordinateSystem": "rkaf:unicode-codepoint"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:4871:4875:sha256-4137b01e139589b7a1d3b3fc4da031d8ce5bb415808734e970c3a58ea0e98f0f",
